# Context - Idea Intake

Copy this file to `Context/Context.md` and fill in what you know. **Only Section 1 is required.** Leave anything else empty, or write "I don't know": the Agent will ask you about it step by step in Discovery Mode instead of guessing.

You may write in any language. Paste raw material (notes, emails, chat logs, links) into Section 10.

---

## 1. Idea (Required)

Describe the idea in two or three sentences: what it is, who it is for, and why it matters.

>

## 2. Project Setup

| Field | Your Answer | Options And Hints |
|---|---|---|
| Project Name | | A working name is fine. |
| Project Profile | | `PERSONAL` (only you), `TEAM` (2+ people building together), `SME` (a business or start-up). |
| Complexity Tier | | `1` small (up to 3 user types, up to 10 features), `2` medium, `3` large or regulated. Leave empty if unsure. |
| Output Language | | `en`, `vi`, or another language. IDs and statuses stay in English. |
| Approver | | Who approves the documents. For PERSONAL, usually you. |
| Reviewers | | Who reviews the documents, or None. |
| Assumption Policy | | `ask` (default: the Agent always asks) or `allow-minor` (the Agent may propose minor assumptions for later confirmation). |
| Documents Needed | | Any of: `BRS`, `BRD` (business), `StRS`, `PRD` (users and product), `SRS` (software), `Backlog`, `Release Plan` (optional). Leave empty for a recommendation. |
| Save Documents To | | A folder path. Leave empty to use `ProjectDocuments/<ProjectName>/`. |
| PRD Covers | | Whole product, one release, or one feature. Only if a PRD is needed. |
| User Stories / Backlog / Release Plan | | `yes` or `no` for each. Any `yes` gives a Standard PRD; all `no` gives a Lean PRD. |

## 3. Problem

What problem does this solve? Who has the problem, and how do they deal with it today?

>

## 4. Goals And Success

What should be true in 6 to 12 months if this succeeds? How will you measure it (numbers and dates if possible)?

>

## 5. Users

Which types of people will use it? What do they need to accomplish?

>

## 6. Main Features

List the main things the product should do. Mark the ones that are essential for the first release.

>

## 7. Constraints

Budget, deadline, team size and skills, required or forbidden technology, platforms (web, mobile, desktop), languages, regions.

>

## 8. Alternatives And Competitors

What do people use today instead (including spreadsheets or manual work)? How will this be different?

>

## 9. Business And Compliance (For SME, Optional Otherwise)

Customers and market, how the product earns revenue or saves cost, personal data collected, countries of operation, regulated sector (finance, health, education).

>

## 10. Raw Material And Sources

Paste or list notes, meeting minutes, emails, mockups, links, or earlier documents. Give each source a name and date if possible so requirements can be traced to it.

| Source Name | Date Or Version | Type | Location Or Content |
|---|---|---|---|
| | | Notes / Meeting / Email / Mockup / Document / Link | |
